      "text": "The first recorded contact between Japan and China occurs when the Japanese kingdom of Na sends an envoy to the Han dynasty, receiving a gold seal from Emperor Guangwu."
    },
    {
      "date": "0250",
      "headline": "Kofun Period Begins",
      "text": "The Kofun period begins, known for its distinctive burial mounds and the emergence of a centralized state under the Yamato clan."
    },
    {
      "date": "0538",
      "headline": "Introduction of Buddhism",
      "text": "Buddhism is introduced to Japan from Korea, significantly influencing Japanese culture, art, and politics."
    },
    {
      "date": "0710",
      "headline": "Nara Period Begins",
      "text": "The Nara period begins with the establishment of the first permanent capital at Heijo-kyo (modern-day Nara), marking the start of a centralized government."
    },
    {
      "date": "0794",
      "headline": "Heian Period Begins",
      "text": "The Heian period begins with the relocation of the capital to Heian-kyo (modern-day Kyoto), a time noted for its cultural flourishing and the development of a distinct Japanese culture."
    },
    {
      "date": "1185",
      "headline": "Kamakura Shogunate Established",
