      "text": "The tournament was branded as 'UEFA Euro 1996' and was held in England. It was the first tournament to feature 16 teams. Germany won the championship by defeating the Czech Republic 2-1 in the final."
    },
    {
      "date": "2000",
      "headline": "First Co-hosted Tournament",
      "text": "UEFA Euro 2000 was the first tournament to be co-hosted by two countries, Belgium and the Netherlands. France won the tournament, defeating Italy 2-1 in the final with a golden goal."
    },
    {
      "date": "2016",
      "headline": "Expansion to 24 Teams",
      "text": "The tournament expanded to include 24 teams for the first time. UEFA Euro 2016 was held in France, and Portugal won the championship by defeating France 1-0 in the final."
    },
    {
      "date": "2020",
      "headline": "Postponement Due to COVID-19",
      "text": "UEFA Euro 2020 was postponed to 2021 due to the COVID-19 pandemic but retained the name Euro 2020. The tournament was held across multiple cities in Europe, and Italy won the championship by defeating England in a penalty shootout in the final."
