      "text": "Poland, Hungary, and the Czech Republic joined NATO, marking the first expansion into former Eastern Bloc countries."
    },
    {
      "date": "2001-09-12",
      "headline": "Article 5 Invoked for the First Time",
      "text": "Following the September 11 attacks in the United States, NATO invoked Article 5 of the North Atlantic Treaty, which states that an attack against one ally is considered an attack against all allies."
