      "date": "2021-01-06",
      "headline": "Fatalities and Injuries",
      "text": "Within 36 hours of the attack, five people died: one was shot by Capitol Police, another died of a drug overdose, and three died of natural causes. Additionally, 174 police officers were injured."
    },
    {
      "date": "2021-01-07",
      "headline": "Death of Officer Brian Sicknick",
      "text": "Capitol Police officer Brian Sicknick died of natural causes a day after being assaulted by rioters during the attack."
    },
    {
      "date": "2021-01-07",
      "headline": "Certification of Election Results",
      "text": "Despite the attack, Congress reconvened and certified the Electoral College results, confirming Joe Biden as the President-elect."
    },
    {
      "date": "2021-01-13",
      "headline": "Second Impeachment of Donald Trump",
      "text": "The House of Representatives impeached President Donald Trump for the second time, charging him with incitement of insurrection related to the Capitol attack."
    },
    {
      "date": "2021-02-13",
      "headline": "Senate Acquits Donald Trump",
      "text": "The Senate acquitted Donald Trump in his second impeachment trial, with 57 senators voting to convict and 43 voting to acquit, falling short of the two-thirds majority needed."
    },
    {
      "date": "2021-07",
      "headline": "Suicides of Responding Officers",
      "text": "Four police officers who responded to the Capitol attack died by suicide within seven months of the incident."
    },
    {
