      "headline": "Formation of Bharatiya Janata Party",
      "text": "The Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) was founded on April 6, 1980, following the dissolution of the Janata Party. The BJP was established as a right-wing party with a focus on Hindu nationalism and was closely associated with the Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh (RSS)."
    },
    {
      "date": "1996",
      "headline": "First Time in Power",
      "text": "The BJP emerged as the largest party in the Lok Sabha elections and formed a government under Atal Bihari Vajpayee. However, the government lasted only 13 days as they could not secure a majority."
    },
    {
      "date": "1998-03",
      "headline": "Formation of National Democratic Alliance",
      "text": "The BJP led the formation of the National Democratic Alliance (NDA), a coalition of parties, and formed the government with Atal Bihari Vajpayee as Prime Minister. This government lasted until 1999."
    },
    {
      "date": "1999-10",
      "headline": "Re-election and Stable Government",
      "text": "The BJP-led NDA won the general elections and formed a stable government with Atal Bihari Vajpayee as Prime Minister, which lasted its full term until 2004."
    },
    {
      "date": "2004",
      "headline": "Defeat in General Elections",
      "text": "The BJP-led NDA was defeated in the 2004 general elections by the Indian National Congress-led United Progressive Alliance (UPA)."
    },
    {
      "date": "2014-05-26",
      "headline": "Narendra Modi Becomes Prime Minister",
      "text": "The BJP won a majority in the 2014 general elections, and Narendra Modi was sworn in as the Prime Minister of India. This marked the first time since 1984 that a single party had won a majority on its own."
    },
    {
      "date": "2019-05-30",
      "headline": "Re-election of Narendra Modi",
      "text": "The BJP won the 2019 general elections with an increased majority, and Narendra Modi was re-elected as Prime Minister of India."
    },
    {
      "date": "2020",
      "headline": "Largest Political Party",
      "text": "By 2020, the BJP had become the largest political party in India in terms of representation in the Parliament of India as well as state legislatures."
    }
  ]
}

