      "headline": "Founding of Los Angeles",
      "text": "Los Angeles was founded by Spanish governor Felipe de Neve on September 4, 1781. It was originally named El Pueblo de Nuestra Señora la Reina de los Ángeles de Porciúncula."
    },
    {
      "date": "1848",
      "headline": "Treaty of Guadalupe Hidalgo",
      "text": "The Treaty of Guadalupe Hidalgo was signed, ending the Mexican-American War. As a result, Los Angeles and the rest of California were ceded to the United States."
    },
    {
      "date": "1850-04-04",
      "headline": "Incorporation as a City",
      "text": "Los Angeles was incorporated as a municipality on April 4, 1850, just five months before California achieved statehood."
    },
    {
      "date": "1876",
      "headline": "Completion of the Southern Pacific Railroad",
      "text": "The completion of the Southern Pacific Railroad connected Los Angeles with the rest of the United States, facilitating growth and development."
    },
    {
      "date": "1892",
      "headline": "Discovery of Oil",
      "text": "Oil was discovered in Los Angeles in 1892, leading to a boom in the local economy and rapid population growth."
    },
    {
      "date": "1913",
      "headline": "Opening of the Los Angeles Aqueduct",
      "text": "The Los Angeles Aqueduct was completed, providing a vital water supply to the city and enabling further expansion."
    },
    {
      "date": "1923",
      "headline": "Hollywood Sign Erected",
      "text": "The iconic Hollywood Sign was erected in 1923, originally reading 'Hollywoodland' as an advertisement for a local real estate development."
    },
    {
      "date": "1932",
      "headline": "1932 Summer Olympics",
      "text": "Los Angeles hosted the 1932 Summer Olympics, marking the first time the city hosted the Olympic Games."
    },
    {
      "date": "1942",
      "headline": "Zoot Suit Riots",
      "text": "The Zoot Suit Riots occurred in Los Angeles in 1942, highlighting racial tensions between servicemen and Mexican American youths."
    },
    {
      "date": "1965",
      "headline": "Watts Riots",
      "text": "The Watts Riots broke out in Los Angeles in 1965, lasting six days and resulting in 34 deaths and over 1,000 injuries."
    },
    {
      "date": "1984",
      "headline": "1984 Summer Olympics",
      "text": "Los Angeles hosted the 1984 Summer Olympics, becoming the only city in the United States to host the event twice."
    },
    {
      "date": "1992",
      "headline": "Los Angeles Riots",
      "text": "The Los Angeles Riots erupted in 1992 following the acquittal of police officers involved in the beating of Rodney King, resulting in widespread violence and destruction."
    },
    {
